1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,543
Welcome to Discrello.

2
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:06,143
In the next few minutes, you will learn how to connect a Trello board to Discord,

3
00:00:06,143 --> 00:00:10,006
so the right person is pinged the moment a card lands in their list.

4
00:00:11,017 --> 00:00:12,115
Here is the idea.

5
00:00:12,115 --> 00:00:17,609
Each Trello list is a stage owned by a role, like script writer, editor, or uploader.

6
00:00:17,609 --> 00:00:20,065
When someone moves a card into a list,

7
00:00:20,065 --> 00:00:25,817
Discrello posts a message in Discord that mentions the person responsible for that stage,

8
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,044
and names the card.

9
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:32,541
Open Discrello in your browser, and sign in with the admin password.

10
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:35,858
First, connect your Discord server.

11
00:00:35,858 --> 00:00:41,333
After inviting the Discrello bot to the server, open Servers, and click Add server.

12
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:43,311
Pick the server from the list.

13
00:00:43,311 --> 00:00:47,796
You can also add an alert channel, where Discrello reports problems.

14
00:00:47,796 --> 00:00:50,038
Save, and the server shows bot OK.

15
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:52,208
Next, open Roles.

16
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:54,524
A role is a stage in your pipeline.

17
00:00:54,524 --> 00:01:00,082
Click New role, enter a short key and a display name, and write the default message.

18
00:01:00,082 --> 00:01:04,648
Placeholders like mention and card title are filled in automatically.

19
00:01:05,683 --> 00:01:08,443
Now choose who gets pinged for this role.

20
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:12,415
Expand the role, and pick a Discord user or a Discord role.

21
00:01:12,415 --> 00:01:15,376
Discrello checks with Discord before saving.

22
00:01:15,376 --> 00:01:19,886
This role is not mentionable, so nobody would actually be notified.

23
00:01:19,886 --> 00:01:23,925
The save is refused, and the message explains how to fix it.

24
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:28,453
Pick a target that works, such as a team member, and save.

25
00:01:28,453 --> 00:01:32,922
Then send a test ping, to confirm that the mention really reaches someone.

26
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:35,698
Now connect a Trello board.

27
00:01:35,698 --> 00:01:37,835
Open Boards, and click Add board.

28
00:01:37,835 --> 00:01:40,619
Paste the board's address, and click Fetch.

29
00:01:40,619 --> 00:01:45,735
Choose the Discord server and the channel for the pings, then create the board.

30
00:01:45,735 --> 00:01:48,778
Discrello registers the Trello webhook for you.

31
00:01:49,783 --> 00:01:52,052
Every list on the board appears here.

32
00:01:52,052 --> 00:01:54,443
Choose the role responsible for a list.

33
00:01:54,443 --> 00:01:57,509
The message is pre-filled from the role's default,

34
00:01:57,509 --> 00:02:00,575
and the preview shows exactly what will be posted.

35
00:02:00,575 --> 00:02:04,683
Click Map list to save, and repeat for each stage of your pipeline.

36
00:02:05,717 --> 00:02:09,581
Use Send test, to post a sample message to the real channel.

37
00:02:10,617 --> 00:02:11,935
That is all the setup.

38
00:02:11,935 --> 00:02:15,409
From now on, when someone moves a card into a mapped list,

39
00:02:15,409 --> 00:02:17,985
the ping arrives in Discord within seconds.

40
00:02:19,017 --> 00:02:22,356
Open Notifications, to see everything Discrello sent:

41
00:02:22,356 --> 00:02:25,191
the card, the list, the role, and the status.

42
00:02:25,191 --> 00:02:27,774
Sent means Discord confirmed the mention.

43
00:02:27,774 --> 00:02:30,609
If a message fails, the reason is shown here,

44
00:02:30,609 --> 00:02:33,570
and you can retry it once the problem is fixed.

45
00:02:34,617 --> 00:02:37,641
The Webhook events tab answers the question:

46
00:02:37,641 --> 00:02:38,947
why didn't it ping?

47
00:02:38,947 --> 00:02:41,489
Every delivery from Trello is listed.

48
00:02:41,489 --> 00:02:46,163
Here, a card moved into a list with no mapping, so nothing was sent.

49
00:02:47,183 --> 00:02:50,973
Finally, Settings shows whether Trello and Discord are connected,

50
00:02:50,973 --> 00:02:53,306
and lets you change the default message.

51
00:02:53,306 --> 00:02:56,396
Discrello re-checks your setup every fifteen minutes,

52
00:02:56,396 --> 00:02:59,486
and warns your alert channel if a permission changes.

53
00:03:00,517 --> 00:03:01,761
That is Discrello.

54
00:03:01,761 --> 00:03:05,631
For more details, see the user guide in the docs folder.

55
00:03:05,631 --> 00:03:07,013
Thanks for watching!
